ver edited by this fix.\n193\t{{- else -}}\n194\tInto the term documents, and nowhere else: the product document's\n195\tstep-phrase catalogue and glossary. A scen-check finding says a phrase\n196\tor a word a Scenario relies on has no stated meaning. The answer is a\n197\tdefinition, written once, where every Scenario using the phrase reads\n198\tit. The Scenario, the generated test rendered from it and the step\n199\tdefinitions are never edited by a scen-check fix. The fix template below\n200\tsays which document, and which kind of entry, the failed check wants.\n201\t{{- end }}\n202\t\n203\t## Subject — Registry Scenario\n204\t\n205\t**Scenario ID:** {{.Subject.ID}}\n206\t**Description:** {{.Subject.Description}}\n207\t**Service:** {{.Subject.Service}}\n208\t**Generated test file:** {{.Subject.Path}}\n209\t\n210\t### Steps\n211\t{{.Subject.FormatSteps}}\n212\t### Lineage — user_stories[]\n213\t{{.Subject.FormatUserStories}}\n214\t## Validation Failure\n215\t\n216\tThe following check failed and needs to be fixed:\n217\t\n218\t### Failed Check: {{ .FailedCheck.SectionPath }}\n219\t\n220\t**Check:** {{ .FailedCheck.Question }}\n221\t**Why it matters:** {{ .FailedCheck.Rationale }}\n222\t**Actual:** {{ .FailedCheck.ActualAnswer }}\n223\t\n224\t**Findings** (one line per failing step or entry):\n225\t{{- range .FailedCheck.Context }}\n226\t- {{ . }}\n227\t{{- end }}\n228\t\n229\t**Fix template:**\n230\t{{ .FailedCheck.FixPrompt }}\n231\t\n232\t## The catalogue\n233\t\n234\tA catalogue entry has four fields:\n235\t\n236\t- `template`: the shape of a step, in the grammar below. It is the\n237\t  entry's identity: no two entries share one.\n238\t- `block`: `given`, `when` or `then`, the one block a step of this shape\n239\t  may sit in.\n240\t- `means`: what a step of this shape means, in product words a reader\n241\t  of the Scenario understands; it may name the template's slots.\n242\t- `terms`: the glossary terms that meaning relies on, each spelled\n243\t  exactly 